sed under the MIT License... covers the software only\"). No art-output grant exists. This exact gap is flagged by the project's own prior work: `docs/design/2026-08-19-vtt-art-license-survey.md:464-466` (\"Project-original rendered-output license: no art-output grant exists yet. Confirm it in the future art section of repository `NOTICE.md`...\"). **Correction required:** the plan must add an explicit new NOTICE.md art section (and manifest `AssetSourceV1.type: 'procedural'` rows) declaring the CC-BY-4.0 (or CC0) grant for generated art bytes before treating \"CC-BY-4.0 self-attribution\" as a fact rather than a to-do.\n\n**A2. \"No external asset families\" is consistent with prior project direction.**\nPARTIALLY DISPROVED as a continuation claim. The survey at `docs/design/2026-08-19-vtt-art-license-survey.md:9-21` explicitly *recommends* a mixed bundle: procedural room/terrain/fog/UI **plus** Game-icons.net (CC-BY-3.0) SVGs for PC/monster tokens, calling pure-procedural token art only \"a total fallback for any fixture actor without an approved glyph\" (line 15, `token.fallback.initial-pattern-v1`). Going pure-procedural for *all* silhouettes, including monster/PC tokens, is a legitimate simplification (it sidesteps the CC-BY-3.0 legal-code/NOTICE.md/dist-emission blocker recorded at lines 23-28 and section D), but it is a **deviation from the prior recommendation**, not a restatement of it. Worth stating explicitly in the plan so a future reader doesn't assume Game-icons.net was silently reintroduced.\n\n**A3. Mutation numbers 51-54 and their names are the project's existing convention.**\nPROVED. They are lifted verbatim from `docs/design/2026-08-19-vtt-art-license-survey.md:325-353` (`asset_without_authorization`, `ccby_attribution_omitted`, `asset_id_resolves_by_filename`, `fixture_fetches_remote_texture`), so continuity with prior design work is real, not invented.\n\n### B. Inventory assumptions\n\n**B1. \"9 existing exports in monsters.ts plus Fighter, Cleric, Wizard, Rogue\" is a like-for-like inventory of 13 statblock-shaped things.**\nDISPROVED as stated. `src/combat/statblocks/monsters.ts:80-189` has exactly 9 `export const … = monsterStatblock({...})` objects (`GOBLIN_WARRIOR`, `HOBGOBLIN_WARRIOR`, `BANDIT_CAPTAIN`, `OGRE`, `PRIEST_ACOLYTE`, `PRIEST`, `SKELETON`, `ZOMBIE`, `WOLF`) — confirmed. But `Fighter`/`Cleric`/`Wizard`/`Rogue` are **not** analogous exported objects; they are class-name string literals used throughout `src/rules/class-*.ts`, `src/domain/enums.ts`, and `src/rules/srd-subclasses.ts` as members of a closed class-name union, with no single \"PC statblock\" export comparable to a `monsterStatblock`. **Correction required:** the plan needs to say explicitly what a \"PC class\" asset row keys off (class-name string brand? the reference-encounter fixture's PC profiles in `src/vtt/reference-encounter.ts`?), because there is no existing 4-item PC export list to mirror the monster module's 9.\n\n**B2. Current reference encounter is 3 PCs + one training brute (4th class art is inventory-only).**\nPROVED. `src/vtt/reference-encounter.ts:59-119` shows a single monster combatant `training-brute` (`REFERENCE_MONSTER_ID`), consistent with \"3 PCs plus one training brute.\" Confirms the 4th class (whichever of Fighter/Cleric/Wizard/Rogue isn't a live reference PC) genuinely has no fixture consumer yet, so \"inventory-only\" is accurate, not a hidden requirement to wire it into the live encounter.\n\n### C. Rendering/integration assumptions\n\n**C1. There is an existing board renderer to extend.**\nPROVED, two of them, and the plan needs to say which (or both). `src/vtt/app.ts` has a canvas-based `#renderBoard`/`#renderBoardUnsafe` (~line 589-714) for the live P2P board. `src/vtt/encounter-app.ts:84-111` has a separate DOM-based `renderBoard()` for the DM-bridge encounter UI, consuming `PlayerBoardProjection`/`DmBoardProjection` from `src/vtt/encounter-projections.ts`. These are architecturally distinct renderers (canvas 2D vs DOM elements) with separate token/fog handling. A plan that says \"the board renderer\" without picking one (or explicitly targeting both) will underspecify scope.\n\n**C2. `ADJUDICATED` styling already exists as a state to hook into.**\nPROVED. `src/vtt/encounter-app.ts:76` (`return 'ADJUDICATED'`), `:111` (`token.dataset.adjudicated`), `:335-336`, `:517`, `:592-593` show adjudicated styling/text already wired through `adjudicatedTargets` from `encounter-projections.ts:75-84`. New asset work should style this existing dataset/attribute hook, not invent a new state channel.\n\n**C3. Fog/active-PC-focus are existing projection-level concepts to style, not new mechanics.**\nPROVED for fog (`projectPlayerBoard` filters `foggedCells` by owned-token visibility, `encounter-projections.ts:100-109`) and for active/highlighted combatant (`highlightedCombatant: visible.activeCombatant`, line 130). This matches the survey's \"focus.active-pc.ink-v1\" / \"fog.hidden/unexplored/revealed.ink-v1\" framing (survey lines 136-139) — good, low-risk assumption.\n\n### D. Build/dist assumptions\n\n**D1. There's an existing dist-cleanliness gate the art manifest checks should extend.**\nPROVED. `tools/assert-dist-clean.mjs` (byte/literal-based scan, chained into `npm run build`) and `tools/licenses/bundled-license-files.ts` (hand-pinned SHA-256 per bundled license file, cross-checked by `tests/unit/licensing/bundled-license-files.test.ts`) are real, active mechanisms exactly matching the pattern the plan wants to extend (mutation 52). This is a solid foundation to reuse rather than build parallel.\n\n**D2. `docs/design/assets-preview` and `tests/unit/assets` are new, not existing paths to be confused for pre-existing conventions.**\nPROVED. Neither directory currently exists (`find`/`ls` both empty). No collision risk, but also no existing convention to match — the plan is creating both from scratch, so their internal layout is unconstrained by precedent and should be specified rather than assumed obvious.\n\n**D3. Untracked `.tmp-*.log` files must remain untouched.**\nPROVED as a constraint to respect — `git status` snapshot shows 8 such files at repo root (`.tmp-audit-findings.log`, `.tmp-lane-3b.log` … `.tmp-lane.log`), pre-existing/unrelated. No plan file path collides with them; no action needed beyond not touching them (and not `git add -A`ing over them if a commit happens later, per repo-wide git safety practice — though this task itself specifies no git operations).\n\n---\n\n### Required plan corrections (summary)\n\n1. **Add an explicit NOTICE.md art-output license grant** (new section, e.g. \"Project-original art (CC-BY-4.0)\") before mutation-52-style checks can have anything real to compare against — currently there is nothing to compare.\n2. **State the PC-class asset key explicitly** — there is no existing 4-object PC export list mirroring `monsters.ts`; decide and document what identifies a \"Fighter\" asset row (class-name literal, a new PC-profile constant, etc.).\n3. **Name which board renderer(s)** (`src/vtt/app.ts` canvas renderer vs `src/vtt/encounter-app.ts` DOM renderer, or both) the new asset resolver integrates into — they are structurally different and both currently exist.\n4. **State explicitly that this plan supersedes/narrows** the survey's recommended mixed-bundle (procedural map + Game-icons.net tokens) to pure-procedural-only, so a future reader doesn't read the two documents as contradictory.","ttft_ms":1902,"ttft_stream_ms":1041,"time_to_request_ms":19,"type":"result","duration_ms":83868,"uuid":"c7eb7028-2657-4827-acf9-13f4b9ce7f2f"}

