+UNIT: vtt-inc8-procedural-pixel-art
+IMPLEMENTER=CODEX (project default). REVIEWER=CLAUDE Sonnet. Risk: moderate, reversible code/assets, no DB/security/external side effects. No commit/push/git operations. Authoritative verification is the supervisor rerun listed below. Existing unrelated .tmp-*.log files are forbidden and untouched.
+
+Binding requirements: the user's direct increment-8 dispatch plus docs/design/2026-08-19-vtt-phase2-movement-controllers.md increment 8, as amended in that direct dispatch to PURE PROCEDURAL ONLY, CC-BY-4.0 self-attribution, and pixel-art silhouettes. The checkout's decisions.md does not contain the user's cited D316.1/D317.8, but a genuine current owner prompt is direct authority for this unit. It explicitly rejects and supersedes docs/design/2026-08-19-vtt-art-license-survey.md's earlier Game-icons recommendation; no claim is made that the older survey itself rejected Game-icons.
+
+Proved assumptions: exactly nine starter monster exports exist in src/combat/statblocks/monsters.ts; the live reference encounter has Fighter/Cleric/Wizard and one training brute; Rogue is inventory-only; CC-BY-4.0 legal code already ships but project art lacks an explicit output grant; src/vtt/encounter-app.ts is the package-consuming phase-2 DOM renderer and is the renderer in scope; the separate generic phase-1 canvas in src/vtt/app.ts has no encounter-package contract and remains unchanged; baseline combat/VTT 1341, sim 176, both tsgo configs green. Player projection must continue to omit foggedCells.
+
+Step 1 — procedural catalog + authorization, one invariant bundle:
+- Add branded stable AssetId, checked-in 16x16 sprite/tile input definitions for 9 starter monsters + Fighter/Cleric/Wizard/Rogue and map/terrain/fog/focus/adjudicated components, and a pure deterministic SVG renderer using crisp-edge integer geometry. No fetch, URL, external source, random, clock, canvas, or filename lookup.
+- Add manifest rows for every output: schema/generator version, fixed input identity/digest, kind, CC-BY-4.0 authorization, self-attribution, output path and digest. Decode/validate unique stable ids, licenses, generator metadata and safe local output paths. Runtime resolver accepts only AssetId and invokes the procedural renderer by input id; filenames are manifest metadata only.
+- Add an exact project-original starter-art notice file, a matching NOTICE.md grant, dist emission through the existing bundled-license path and legal-page reachability. Extend the plain-node dist digest guard for the notice.
+- Add the deterministic generator tool and materialize outputs under public/assets/art plus a docs/design/assets-preview/starter-art-board.svg fixture preview. All materialized bytes come from the same pure renderer and fixed inputs.
+
+Step 2 — package and phase-2 renderer consumption:
+- Add a Zod encounter-art/package schema whose map, terrain, fog, UI, and combatant-token fields are branded AssetIds and validate every reference through the manifest resolver. Add a reference package mapping live Fighter/Cleric/Wizard/training-brute to stable sprite ids.
+- Add a pure encounter-board render-model module producing ordered cells/layers from a projection and decoded package. Update src/vtt/encounter-app.ts to delegate every board cell to that model and render its floor/terrain/token/fog/focus/adjudicated SVG data URIs inline through asset ids, with no runtime fetch. DM-only fog uses dmOnly.foggedCells; the player board receives no fog coordinates. Update CSS for pixel-art layering while preserving labels and existing DOM state hooks.
+
+Step 3 — independent gates and controls in new tests/unit/assets plus existing allowed suites:
+- Mutation 51: manifest decoder rejects missing/non-CC-BY-4.0 authorization and proves every checked-in art output is owned exactly once.
+- Mutation 52: derived exact art notice equals NOTICE.md section, legal screen output, bundled dist asset bytes, and plain-node dist guard pin. New tests/unit/assets tests directly exercise these changed legal/dist modules because the user's gate excludes the pre-existing licensing/UI suites.
+- Mutation 53: a renamed output path with unchanged id still resolves/renders identically; filename lookup is unavailable.
+- Mutation 54: static scan of runtime renderer/resolver/package/board path rejects fetch, XMLHttpRequest, http(s), remote src/CSS url; render succeeds with a throwing global fetch sentinel.
+- Determinism: render twice from equal fixed inputs for byte equality; independent expected-hash table pins every sprite/output digest and combined sprite inventory digest. Exercise the pure board render model with both player and DM projections: stable-id sprite layers must appear; fog assets only in the DM model; active-PC and ADJUDICATED layers must survive. A wiring sentinel reads encounter-app.ts and requires its delegation to the model, so leaving the legacy token-only renderer in place fails. Verify the two-projection preview exists and contains all required visual-state markers.
+- Authoritative commands: npx vitest run --configLoader runner tests/unit/combat tests/unit/vtt tests/unit/assets ; npx vitest run --configLoader runner --root tools/sim ; npx tsgo -p tsconfig.app.json --noEmit ; npx tsgo -p tsconfig.node.json --noEmit. No DB/schema suite because no DB is touched. Do not run broader/disallowed tests.
+
+Allowed paths: src/assets/**; src/vtt/encounter-package.ts; src/vtt/reference-encounter-art.ts; src/vtt/encounter-board.ts; src/vtt/encounter-app.ts; src/vtt/styles.css; tests/unit/assets/**; tools/assets/**; public/assets/art/**; docs/design/assets-preview/**; docs/licenses/STARTER-ART-NOTICE.txt; NOTICE.md; README.md; tools/licenses/bundled-license-files.ts; tools/assert-dist-clean.mjs; src/ui/screens/legal/legal.ts. Forbidden: everything else, especially DB/schema, src/vtt/app.ts, existing tests, .tmp-*.log, git metadata.
+
+Rollback: remove new catalog/generated paths and revert only the listed integration/license edits; no persisted state or schema changes exist.
